dzn: Lower multiview on Intel instead of using view instancing

Intel's Direct3D 12 driver under WSL2 (a UHD 770) crashes in
CreatePipelineState for any pipeline state with view instancing, so every
multiview pipeline crashed the app (dEQP-VK.multiview.masks.* and the
multiview indirect draws). Dozen's own lowering of the view index, which it
uses where Direct3D 12 has no view instancing, passes them there.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
index f869d51..c90a369 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
@@ -1290,7 +1290,11 @@ dzn_physical_device_create(struct vk_instance *instance,
       goto fail_clean;
    }
 
-   if (dzn_instance->debug_flags & DZN_DEBUG_MULTIVIEW)
+   /* Intel's Direct3D 12 driver under WSL2 (a UHD 770) crashes creating any
+    * pipeline state with view instancing; Dozen's own multiview lowering
+    * works there.
+    */
+   if ((dzn_instance->debug_flags & DZN_DEBUG_MULTIVIEW) || pdev->desc.vendor_id == 0x8086)
       pdev->options3.ViewInstancingTier = D3D12_VIEW_INSTANCING_TIER_NOT_SUPPORTED;
    if (dzn_instance->debug_flags & DZN_DEBUG_NO_16BIT)
       pdev->options4.Native16BitShaderOpsSupported = false;
